;; expect: main.e_only refused absurd_needs_init
;; §8.4 slice 3.27 rule 7, landing 3: a refuted row is Init's absurd applied to a proof and its
;; negation — an L term, read on the typed route and erased to the refuted row. A body read
;; E-first (here: its result is a Symbol, which has no L reading) cannot write one: the pointer
;; names the route, as dif's does.
(fn e_only ((n Nat)) Symbol (if (= n 0) (quote z) (absurd 1 2)))
